        "# Iterable\n",
        "\n",
        "An iterable is an object from which an iterator can be obtained, typically with `iter(obj)`. Lists, strings, and generators are examples of iterables.\n",
        "\n",
        "Source: [Python glossary](https://docs.python.org/3/glossary.html#term-iterable)"
      ]
    }
